WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(upbeat music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.530
- [Narrator] You're in Budapest.

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.400
And you feel like having a drink.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.730
There's vodka, gin, rum, lemonade,

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.550
but this would all be a mistake.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.860
Because in this city, you have to indulge

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.170
in a glassful of Hungarian history.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.370
Well, actually, three to be exact.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.804
Meet Pálinka, Unicum and soda water.

00:00:19.804 --> 00:00:20.637
Mm.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.963
Without further ado, let's
bring in our experts.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.160
First up, Zoltan who heads up

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.030
the House of Hungarian
Pálinka in Budapest.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.540
- Pálinka is a strong spirit.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.220
It is 100 percent fruit distilled.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.800
Pálinka is deeply woven into

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.470
the fabric of Hungarian society.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.170
Everybody knows what it is.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.800
And the history of Pálinka began in 1300s

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.120
when the Queen and the King of Hungary

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.310
were all suffering from gout.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:56.470
They stumbled upon this
earlier version of Pálinka,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.020
which they used to cure themselves.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:02.400
It is made from a huge variety of fruits,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.100
apricots to plums to
cherries to pears to apples.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.300
- [Narrator] Now we've
heard it's quite strong.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.750
- The usual alcohol content is typically

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:17.460
between 40 and 50 percent, some of them 60 percent.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.650
Some of them even higher.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.600
- [Narrator] Can your
Unicum beat that, Sándor?

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.060
- We can't beat it, but we can match it

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.870
because we also have 40 percent.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.950
Really, Unicum is a bitter herbal liquor;

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.340
there's roughly 10 million Hungarians,

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.030
and we sell yearly 4 million bottles.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.720
It was invented in 1790 by my ancestor.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.370
I am the sixth generation.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.770
- [Narrator] See this
doctor was the physician

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.910
to the Emperor of Austria-Hungary.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.920
And when the Emperor had a bad stomach.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.720
- My ancestor made him Unicum,

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.470
which is made of 40 different
kinds of herbs and spices.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.120
The recipe's a secret,
so I can tell you that,

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.977
for example, we use vanilla or ginger.

00:01:58.977 --> 00:02:00.763
OK, I told you two.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.356
That's enough.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.800
(laughs)

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.360
- [Narrator] And for you
non-drinkers, there's soda water.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.660
A staple on Hungarian tables.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.207
This is László and his father.

00:02:11.207 --> 00:02:14.660
(speaking foreign language)

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:15.792
- [Narrator] Thank you, gentlemen.

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:19.459
(speaking foreign language)

00:02:35.652 --> 00:02:37.090
No wonder László knows his stuff.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.050
It was in Hungary where
the large scale production

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.461
of soda water started.

00:02:40.461 --> 00:02:44.378
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:58.825 --> 00:03:00.492
Shall we taste them?

00:03:03.226 --> 00:03:05.170
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.173
Bottom's up, gents.

00:03:07.066 --> 00:03:08.450
- That was strong.
- That's a good drink.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.867
- That was great.

